WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.776
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will put the right resgrid

00:00:04.776 --> 00:00:09.551
app on each device. A configured department still needs members and shared devices

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:14.327
to sign in to the correct department with the correct permissions. We will

00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:19.103
explain the features, the setup decisions, and a practical way to check the

00:00:19.103 --> 00:00:19.470
result.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.867
Members install the Responder app, a tablet in Engine 1 runs the Unit

00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:29.663
app and a station screen shows the Big Board. Most members use Resgrid

00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:34.460
through the Responder app. Getting everyone installed and signed in is what lets

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:39.256
dispatches reach them. The examples in this series use a fictional department and

00:00:39.256 --> 00:00:41.470
are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:48.391
Responder application. The member app for receiving dispatches, responding and setting status. Have

00:00:48.391 --> 00:00:53.740
every member install the Responder app, sign in and allow notifications.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.856
Unit application. The in-vehicle app that represents an apparatus. Install the Unit app

00:00:59.856 --> 00:01:03.250
on each apparatus tablet and select its unit.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:09.299
Dispatch application. The dispatcher view for creating and managing calls. Give dispatch access

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:13.490
to the people who dispatch, then have them sign in.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:20.220
Incident command and accountability. Incident command and accountability for incident commanders. Give command

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.520
access to the officers who run incidents.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.732
Big Board. A station display of calls, units and personnel. Open the Big

00:01:28.732 --> 00:01:32.280
Board on a station screen and choose what it shows.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.430
Dashboard. The department home page: current status, staffing and activity. Decide which devices

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:43.980
each role will use and share the app download links with your members.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:50.275
My Profile. Your own profile, contact details and notification preferences. Decide which devices

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:55.970
each role will use and share the app download links with your members.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:01.448
Your Departments. Switch between the departments you belong to. Decide which devices each

00:02:01.448 --> 00:02:05.950
role will use and share the app download links with your members.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:11.883
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Set up a

00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:17.216
member device with Responder and notification permissions. Step 2. Set up an apparatus

00:02:17.216 --> 00:02:22.548
tablet with Unit and select its unit. Step 3. Grant appropriate Dispatch or

00:02:22.548 --> 00:02:25.830
Command access and configure a station Big Board.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:32.239
Now verify the result. Check the active department, device identity, and a controlled

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:38.047
notification test. Check what a shared station screen exposes. A common problem to

00:02:38.047 --> 00:02:43.856
watch for: Installing an app does not prove alerts arrive. Verify OS notification

00:02:43.856 --> 00:02:47.430
and location settings on the actual device used.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:53.306
Your practice task is simple. Use a sample member, unit tablet, dispatcher, and

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:58.583
station display to follow the same training incident. Record which devices complete the

00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:03.859
test. Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be

00:03:03.859 --> 00:03:08.730
reviewed. Use the linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

